<title>BRAZIL: Brazil may let pension funds invest in derivatives.</title>
<headline>Brazil may let pension funds invest in derivatives.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil may allow pension funds to invest directly in derivatives to hedge their portfolios, financial newspaper Gazeta Mercantil said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;I think the derivatives may be used by the pension funds as hedge instruments to secure their investments,&quot; Antonio Fernando Gazzoni, an official at the Social Security Ministry, was quoted as saying.</p>
<p>The proposal is under study by the ministry and the Central Bank, the newspaper added. --Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo Newsroom 5511 2485412</p>
</text>
